message: "If you use this software, its methods, or its results in research, please cite the software release and the relevant research paper."
title: "ksdft2effmass: Controlled reduction of Kohn–Sham DFT operators to effective-mass models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ragasa
    given-names: "Eugene J."
    affiliation: "Department of Physics, De La Salle University, Taft Campus, Manila, Philippines"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3856-734X"
abstract: >-
  Research software for constructing and validating reductions of
  first-principles Kohn–Sham Hamiltonians into lattice and effective-mass
  models, beginning with phosphorus and boron impurities in silicon.
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/eragasa/ksdft2effmass.git"
url: "https://github.com/eragasa/ksdft2effmass"
keywords:
  - density-functional theory
  - Kohn–Sham Hamiltonian
  - effective-mass theory
  - Wannier functions
  - impurity operators
  - silicon
  - research software
